          "text": "**Epilepsy Clinic Letter**\n\n**Re:** E003  \n**Clinic:** Epilepsy Service  \n\nDear Colleague,\n\nThank you for referring this patient for epilepsy review.\n\nThe current clinical information is consistent with **generalized epilepsy**. Seizures are occurring approximately **once per week**. No further seizure semiology, precipitating factors, medication history, or investigation results were provided for this review.\n\nThe ongoing weekly seizure frequency indicates that seizure control is not yet adequate. A detailed review of seizure type, adherence, potential triggers, antiseizure medication history, and relevant investigations—including EEG and brain imaging where clinically indicated—is recommended.\n\nThe patient should continue standard seizure-safety precautions, including avoiding driving in accordance with local regulations and taking care around bathing, swimming, heights, and open flames. They should seek urgent medical attention for a seizure lasting five minutes or longer, repeated seizures without recovery, serious injury, or breathing difficulty.\n\nFollow-up with the epilepsy service is recommended to confirm the generalized epilepsy syndrome and guide treatment adjustment.\n\nYours sincerely,  \n\n**Epilepsy Clinic**",
